  "configuration_id": "config_002",
  "reason": "Evidence: PCA (pca_n2000) with singleprofile RNA is the best configuration so far (acc=0.485), outperforming scgpt RNA (0.411) and image-only ResNet50 (0.208). The image modality appears weak, so the most promising direction is improving the RNA pipeline. Uncertainty: We have not yet tested whether multiprofile representation (with aggregation) can improve upon singleprofile for the best-performing encoder. This experiment tests config_002, which changes only the profile setting from single to multi (with avgpool aggregation) while keeping the proven PCA encoder. This isolates the effect of multiprofile aggregation on the top RNA baseline. It is the best use of experiment 4 because it is a minimal, single-variable extension of our best result, directly informing whether to invest remaining budget in multiprofile variants (transformer aggregation) or multimodal fusion, or to pivot toward alternative encoders."
}

